  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r25_1126_100\r25_1126_103\r25_1126_104\r25_1126_105\r25_1126_106\rLocation Plan\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that match the existing building or as specified in the approved application.\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation of the HMO, Cycle parking, shall be provided as indicated on drawing 25_1126_100, in accordance with the following requirements:\r\r- Provision of a minimum of SIX long stay cycle parking spaces;\r\r- in an accessible location; the store door must have a minimum opening width of 1.2m\r\r- long stay cycle parking spaces secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\r- fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area\r",
    "Prior to occupation of the development, the refuse storage facilities shown on drawing number 25_1126_100 shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area\r",
    "No cooking facilities, including hot plates, shall be installed in the bedrooms of the development hereby permitted unless details have first been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Any cooking facilities shall thereafter only be implemented in accordance with the details that have been approved pursuant to this condition.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The existing outbuilding shall not be occupied at any time other than for purposes incidental to the HMO as and shall not be used as an independent dwelling or as a bedroom at any time.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development complies with adopted standards, does not impact on neighbouring amenity and is in character with the existing form of development in the locality in accordance with relevant adopted planning policies of the Enfield Local Plan\r"
  ],
